{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end","id":1543390,"title":"Paradox CEO says Bloodlines is a \"Dead End\".","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-08T20:55:36-07:00","id":1543390,"title":"Paradox CEO says Bloodlines is a \"Dead End\".","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/paradox-wants-to-get-out-of-the-rpg-business-if-bloodlines-2-god-willing-is-successful-bloodlines-3-will-be-done-by-someone-else/\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/pa...-someone-else/</a> - It's been nearly a decade since Paradox Interactive acquired White Wolf and the World of Darkness, and nearly as long since it started working with Hard Suit Labs based on its pitch for <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/everything-we-know-about-vampire-the-masqueradebloodlines-2/\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Masquerade \u2013 Bloodlines 2</a>. And boy has it been a rough time.<br /> <br /> After four years working in secret, Hard Suit and Paradox announced Bloodlines 2 in 2019. We'd be playing it in 2020, the pair said. Then it was delayed. And delayed again. The 2020 target became 2021, and then it was delayed indefinitely, with Hard Suit given the boot.<br /> <br /> For a while, it seemed like cancellation was inevitable. And it did almost end up in the bin. &quot;If we hadn't found The Chinese Room,&quot; deputy CEO Mattias Lilja tells me, &quot;and seen what they'd done with the early work, [cancellation] would have been the next logical step, because we could not continue as we did.&quot;<br /> <br /> Lilja believes it's in a better place now\u2014though it was <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/rpg/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-has-been-delayed-again-this-time-to-add-more-endings-to-the-game-along-with-some-extra-polish/\" target=\"_blank\">recently struck with yet another delay</a>, pushing it out of 2024 and into the first half of 2025. &quot;It's been in development a very long time, but we are starting to see the game shape up to be something we can\u2026 we think it will be a World of Darkness experience.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's strangely tepid praise, but also refreshing. The reason for this interview was not the usual marketing-driven fare. No big announcements. No hype. Just a rather frank explanation about what's going on at Paradox, the reasons why it's been struggling recently, and what it's doing to change its fortunes. But even with that in mind, there seems to be a bit of nervousness about how Bloodlines 2 will ultimately be received. And it's not something that Paradox wants to go through again.<br /> <br /> &quot;It is not in our strategic direction to make this kind of game,&quot; Lilja says. &quot;So if Bloodlines 2, God willing, is successful, Bloodlines 3 [will be] done by someone else, on the license from us. I would say it's the sort of strategic way this would work. So it's still an outlier from what we're supposed to do, we don't know that stuff, so we should probably let other people do it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Paradox has its own small-scale experimental label, Paradox Arc, where it can try different things, but a big RPG doesn't remotely fit that. It would have to be something &quot;very different&quot;, says Lilja, like a CRPG, but even that's a &quot;big investment&quot;, and nowadays expectations are higher than ever thanks to Baldur's Gate 3. So &quot;regardless of outcome,&quot; he says, Bloodlines is a &quot;dead end&quot;.<br /> <br /> As for the future of Bloodlines 2, specifically: &quot;We don't drop games. We make sure they work. We make sure they fulfil the promise that they have. The rest is very much up to the players.&quot; So you can expect the usual slate of updates and fixes, but DLC? I wouldn't hold your breath.<br /> <br /> &quot;I think some studios do strategic investments, long term things, because they feel that the cost of not doing it is too high. But, I mean, I think it's fairly clear, at least to me, and I think to you, even in the best of cases, Bloodlines does not have a super long shelf life. That's not the way these games behave. You have an influx of players, there's a bit of word of mouth, and they have a high peak, and then they trail off. And it's not the type of gameplay that develops over time that much. So I think that's part of why these types of games are not really that attractive to us.&quot;<br /> <br /> Yet it was the persistence of Bloodlines' fans that inspired this sequel, 20 years after the original. Better supported RPGs, meanwhile, can keep going year after year, as evidenced by the incredibly long life of Bethesda RPGs. And then there's Baldur's Gate\u2014a 26-year-old series that's just spawned its third game, which in turn has been one of Steam's most played games for over a year, despite the lack of DLC. Some RPGs have an incredibly long tail. But it is clear they aren't in Paradox's wheelhouse, and passing the licence to other caretakers might be the smart call here. </div> </div> </div>The CEO saying that Bloodlines is a 'dead end' and writing off a hypothetical Bloodlines 3 isn't exactly instilling me with very good expectations for part 2. Honestly it sounds like the CEO doesn't have any interest in the WoD IP whatsoever. At this point, I'm kind of hoping they sell the IP to someone else who has more desire to work with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T21:54:08-07:00","id":1543392,"title":"","content":"It seems like most of the people who were interested in it about nine years ago aren't there anymore. I'm not sure if it's the case, but they certainly started to dwindle in 2018.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T22:02:47-07:00","id":1543393,"title":"","content":"That sounds quite dire... Seems like Bloodlines 2 will fit perfectly into this pattern as I feared:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1537219-it-s-official-i-am-abandoning-wod5?p=1538120#post1538120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think Paradox as a company is a bad one. It's only thanks to a few of their games which are these juggernauts on the market that they stay profitable. Aside from those, namely Hearts of Iron IV, Crusader Kings 3 and Stellaris, Paradox as a company would be in a world of trouble. If there's anything that has been a constant in the last few years, it's them fucking up as a publisher.<br /> <br /> Let's go over some of the highlights over the last few years:<ul><li>Lamplighter's Leauge: Paradox had high hopes for the game and Harebrained Games are a good developer (they made those isometric Shadowrun games, for example). But months before the launch, thanks to a lack of support from Paradox 80% of the staff at the studio were let go. Then the game got released to middling reviews (mostly because of the bugs and lack of content) and then Paradox had to announce that it considered <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/paradox-says-the-lamplighters-league-sales-were-a-big-disappointment-confirms-recent-layoffs-at-developer-harebrained-schemes/\" target=\"_blank\">the game a failure</a>. And it doesn't seem like there's any more content planned for it.</li> <li>City Skylines 2: That game launched in a disastrous state. Just google it. A complete failure. The developers are still busy trying to crawl out of that hole and win back the goodwill of the players...</li> <li>Star Trek Infinite: One of the more popular mods for their Sci-Fi-grand strategy game Stellaris revolves around Star Trek. And so Paradox thought: Hey, let's have someone develop an official version. And that's Star Trek Infinite except... the fan-mods are simply better. The game launches, disappoints (middling reviews, lack of interest, sales...) and six months after launch it's announced that <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/paradoxs-grand-strategy-star-trek-infinite-will-receive-no-further-updates\" target=\"_blank\">Paradox will stop any support for the game</a>. In other words, Paradox isn't paying the devs to patch the game or make DLC for it.</li> <li>Life By You: It was pitched as a new Sims-type life-building game. They even created a studio for it called Tectone. Well, a month ago or so, Paradox announced it had decided to <a href=\"https://news.cision.com/paradox-interactive-ab/r/paradox-interactive-cancels-the-release-of-life-by-you-which-impacts-the-second-quarter-with-msek-20,c4002478\" target=\"_blank\">cancel the game</a>. This game had been in development since 2019. Five years of development, a whole studio of developers and 19 million dollars in investment... all flushed down the toilet. Ah, yeah, they closed the studio Tectone as well on top of that.</li> <li>Prison Architect 2: Despite previous delays, the game's release-date is now changed to &quot;unknown&quot;. It seems like there's still a lot of work ahead for the developers. (source: <a href=\"https://www.pcgamer.com/games/strategy/paradox-indefinitely-delays-prison-architect-2-just-like-it-did-with-life-by-you-before-it-was-scrapped/\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Paradox indefinitely delays Prison Architect 2, just like it did with Life By You before it was scrapped&quot;</a>)</li> </ul><br /> Bloodlines 2 turning out to be a failure wouldn't be that surprising.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the future of Bloodlines 2, specifically: &quot;We don't drop games. We make sure they work. We make sure they fulfil the promise that they have. The rest is very much up to the players.&quot; So you can expect the usual slate of updates and fixes, but DLC? I wouldn't hold your breath </div> </div> </div>Look at what I outlined above. This is what this means: Paradox isn't interested in paying The Chinese Room to patch the game and/or develop DLC for it. As the examples above show, Paradox has no problem whatsoever with abandoning games very quickly after release. Already musing about what Bloodlines 3 could be like is a very bad sign. I also feel really bad for the people at The Chinese Room who I imagine are working very hard right now to meet the new release date for Bloodlines 2 next year. Because as the examples above also show, you know what will happen to those people once the game gets released: They'll get fired. Because Paradox isn't interested in paying them to patch the game and/or develop DLC. And The Chinese Room studio is more focused on walking-simulator/first-person-horror-type-games like Still Wakes The Deep so they don't need developers who do RPG-action/stealth-stuff.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I think some studios do strategic investments, long term things, because they feel that the cost of not doing it is too high. But, I mean, I think it's fairly clear, at least to me, and I think to you, even in the best of cases, Bloodlines does not have a super long shelf life. That's not the way these games behave. You have an influx of players, there's a bit of word of mouth, and they have a high peak, and then they trail off. And it's not the type of gameplay that develops over time that much. So I think that's part of why these types of games are not really that attractive to us.&quot; </div> </div> </div>This is also troubling because this CEO sounds like yet another dumbass who has fully bought into the idea that live-service-games are the future and a rich goldmine. And all you have to do is look at Concord and this year's Suicide Squad game to know that this is just pure delusion. But if Paradox is led by an idiot who seems to have stuck his head in the sand and doesn't know where the wind is blowing... Well, I'm not surprised then that as far as publishing is concerned all you get from Paradox is a series of failures.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T22:29:34-07:00","id":1543394,"title":"","content":"Just a small note: Lilja is the deputy CEO, not the full CEO who is still Wester (a key figure in Paradox's decision to buy the WoD IP in the first place).<br /> <br /> Though I read that statement about shelf life very differently (though still very corpo speak misguided). People are still playing BL 1... there are fans making patches and mods for it still. Lilja seems to think that BL doesn't have the potential for duration like Paradox's core portfolio where people keep playing games for a long time... even though BL 1 is a flat refutation that action RPGs can't have the same kind of longevity as 4X and other procedural generated games that extend replayability via randomized starts/etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T22:51:39-07:00","id":1543396,"title":"","content":"Disappointing but hardly unexpected that game development problems keep cropping up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-08T23:16:19-07:00","id":1543400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543394#post1543394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just a small note: Lilja is the deputy CEO, not the full CEO who is still Wester (a key figure in Paradox's decision to buy the WoD IP in the first place).<br /> <br /> Though I read that statement about shelf life very differently (though still very corpo speak misguided). People are still playing BL 1... there are fans making patches and mods for it still. Lilja seems to think that BL doesn't have the potential for duration like Paradox's core portfolio where people keep playing games for a long time... even though BL 1 is a flat refutation that action RPGs can't have the same kind of longevity as 4X and other procedural generated games that extend replayability via randomized starts/etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it suggests that he doesn't really understand the game or genre to begin with. While not on the level of Baldur's Gate 1&amp;2, Bloodlines still has a pretty massive fan scene behind it and a lot of cultural cache within the cRPG community. Taking a quick peek over at Nexusmods, it looks like people have released a couple of dozen mods for the game just this year. <br /> <br /> It's also unfortunate that Paradox has never shown any interest in using the IP elsewhere. For example, it wouldn't be hard to imagine a Grand Strategy game in the vein of Crusader Kings using the VtM Dark Ages setting. Paradox could do something like that, if they wanted, but apparently they don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T01:38:22-07:00","id":1543402,"title":"","content":"Usually, companies tend to try to hide when their game's development isn't going well. So the fact that a person in a position of authority is THIS pessimistic about BL2's prospects...that's a REALLY bad sign.<br /> <br /> Nine years. Nine years, for what?<br /> <br /> Paradox never should have acquired the World of Darkness IP. Full stop. It's been an unmitigated disaster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T02:48:44-07:00","id":1543407,"title":"","content":"Not to be too forgiving here, but despite the tone we really haven't learned that much. Paradox was never planning on doing that much in-house, because they're not that big of a video game company. They were always planning on getting more studios with more experience in specific game styles to do the majority of the work for their brand; just like how even when they started a WW subsidiary way back when, they were talking about doing core development in house and then shopping the license out to other TTRPG makers to fill out the game lines. Saying that BL isn't Paradox's kinda of video game rings pretty hollow when Paradox up and bought a studio to add to their portfolio that does action cRPGs just to do the first iteration of BL 2.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the frankness coming from such a high level c-suite level person seems to be something different from what's being said: Paradox has found out they really don't like being in the brand management business. It seems like they really misjudged the level of internal resources to develop and maintain the core brand identity to the point where they can make deals with existing studios to make X style of game while following Paradox's V5/WoD setting bible and style guides and then not be highly involved in the production of the game. Managing a brand that's going to feel cohesive across TTRPGs, IF games, action cRPG games, comics, and who knows what else is not easy; even if you're hiring other people to do the vast majority of the actual work to make the individual products happen.<br /> <br /> The whole article feels like they're giving up and just planning to let studios to make whatever games they make as long as the pitch is good enough. While in general that's not a good idea because it leads to brand dilution and so on, it's a lot easier on their internal teams and at least in the short term could be profitable enough to make shareholders happen with the initial purchase before whatever Paradox does with the IPs after nobody really wants to make new games for them anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude1e","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T04:05:56-07:00","id":1543411,"title":"","content":"Paradox is in a bad place right now. Everything's either getting canceled or delayed. Recently it was also announced that the DLC for City: Skylines 2 would also get <a href=\"https://www.eurogamer.net/cities-skylines-2-dlc-gets-further-delays-as-developer-priorities-assets-editor-for-mods\" target=\"_blank\">delayed</a>. Except for their core-brands (their grand strategy games), nothing seems to be working out in the way they hoped. This article feels more like an attempt to deal with the current problems by lowering expectations for the near future.<br /> <br /> What I could see is that this is where the new direction is described:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Paradox has its own small-scale experimental label, Paradox Arc, where it can try different things, but a big RPG doesn't remotely fit that. It would have to be something &quot;very different&quot;, says Lilja, like a CRPG, but even that's a &quot;big investment&quot;, and nowadays expectations are higher than ever thanks to Baldur's Gate 3. So &quot;regardless of outcome,&quot; he says, Bloodlines is a &quot;dead end&quot;. </div> </div> </div>So the idea is that you won't even get games on the scale of an Earthblood, a Swansong or that Justice VR game anymore. It's just going to be small &quot;indie&quot;-style games like visual novels or those text-adventures from here on out. And Paradox would settle for that rather than trying to do anything big with the WOD IP.<br /> <br /> But I guess, we'll see what happens after Bloodlines 2 gets released.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T13:19:53-07:00","id":1543435,"title":"","content":"Somewhere out there, there is an alternate reality where both CofD and WoD are in the hands of a company that cares about them. Not super invested in Bloodlines, but this is hugely disappointing for its fanbase and that sucks.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543402#post1543402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Usually, companies tend to try to hide when their game's development isn't going well. So the fact that a person in a position of authority is THIS pessimistic about BL2's prospects...that's a REALLY bad sign.<br /> <br /> Nine years. Nine years, for what?<br /> <br /> Paradox never should have acquired the World of Darkness IP. Full stop. It's been an unmitigated disaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly? Given the state of the game and the decision to just ghost the entire CofD fanbase? I think an unmitigated disaster is far to generous an assessment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":4433,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","user":"Second Chances","date":". 10-09-2024, 04:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T13:49:49-07:00","id":1543440,"title":"","content":"This is precisely what I expect out of Paradox given their treatment of the IP lately. They can't even pretend to give a shit any more, and to me, it shows in a lot more than just their treatment of Bloodlines 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T14:32:21-07:00","id":1543448,"title":"","content":"My take from the interview is that Lija is trying to say this was a bad idea from the get go and they didn\u2019t know what they were doing, without sounding too bad. But not realizing that they still don\u2019t know what they\u2019re doing.<br /> <br /> Paradox invested in a lot of things that are outside their core market, but refused to understand how those other markets work, and that didn\u2019t change at all.<br /> <br /> For how much they care about the IP, it\u2019s an internal schism, as it seems. WoD is bad business for them as much as they\u2019re bad business for WoD. As a company, they don\u2019t know shit about how to work this kind of IP. But their CEO wants his toy. It is a pet project and that\u2019s all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T14:57:37-07:00","id":1543450,"title":"","content":"IGN also ran <a href=\"https://www.ign.com/articles/paradox-chinese-room-vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2-sequel-someone-else\" target=\"_blank\">an article about this topic</a> but they seemed to take things a bit too far in their interpretation of what Lilja said, so Paradox reached out to IGN and gave this clarification:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Update: In a follow-up statement to IGN, Lilja clarified, &quot;Paradox is not done with Vampire: the Masquerade. Paradox, as a video game publisher, will not directly focus on publishing too far outside of its core competencies in the long run.&quot;<br /> <br /> He added, &quot;We are very confident in The Chinese Room in developing Bloodlines 2! When we say that \u201ca potential Bloodlines 3 will be done by \u2018someone else,\u2019 we mean Paradox Interactive as the publisher.\u201d<br /> <br /> He concluded, &quot;We continue to own and work with World of Darkness, but that team operates very differently from the core organization.&quot;<br /> <br /> A Paradox spokesperson added that Paradox still owns World of Darkness and plans to continue to support Vampire: The Masquerade. </div> </div> </div>I think that's a good, short summary of what Paradox is trying to say with this press-tour...<br /> <br /> Although, I still find the whole story very unconvincing. Even saying &quot;We found out RPGs aren't in our wheelhouse as a publisher, so we won't do that anymore.&quot;. So what exactly is in their wheelhouse as publishers then? Strategy games? Well, how about the disastrous release of City: Skylines 2 then? By that logic, that should've worked out splendidly because Paradox supposedly knows what they're doing when they deal with strategy games. But that didn't happen. Or is the implication that it's just this one niche of grand-strategy-games? Well, if that's the plan, why even be a publisher...?<br /> <br /> And the way this was presented was also bad in my opinion. Why would you go out there to talk to an outlet about an upcoming game-release and introduce all this doomerism? Describing the upcoming game as a &quot;dead end&quot;, confess to this list of mistakes you've made and say to the people currently working on this upcoming game &quot;If you're expecting to get support from us, the publisher, to work on something like DLC, don't hold your breath.&quot;. It's just a huge heap of negativity. The messaging tries harder to depress than it tries to excite. But why would you want to go to the press with that type of messaging?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T22:11:06-07:00","id":1543491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543450#post1543450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the way this was presented was also bad in my opinion. Why would you go out there to talk to an outlet about an upcoming game-release and introduce all this doomerism? Describing the upcoming game as a &quot;dead end&quot;, confess to this list of mistakes you've made and say to the people currently working on this upcoming game &quot;If you're expecting to get support from us, the publisher, to work on something like DLC, don't hold your breath.&quot;. It's just a huge heap of negativity. The messaging tries harder to depress than it tries to excite. But why would you want to go to the press with that type of messaging?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;So if Bloodlines 2 is, God willing, successful...&quot; Yeah, that doesn't inspire much confidence at all. I honestly can't remember the last time I've seen a company CEO actively shit on their own upcoming product like this. Normally, even if they expect something to do poorly, you at least get a more neutral tone. &quot;Blah blah blah, we expect that it will meet our internal estimates,&quot; or something. Shareholders generally don't like it when management openly talks to the press about how their upcoming product is a complete mess. In fact, the way he quickly contacted IGN (even though IGN's take seemed to be fairly reasonable considering what was said) to try and do damage control suggests that some people were not terribly happy with the blunt message he gave.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-09T23:35:28-07:00","id":1543497,"title":"","content":"I guess a ten year development cycle for a video game can really take the wind out of your sails. If it was going to be released on consoles, it missed a generation and change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T10:49:52-07:00","id":1543531,"title":"","content":"More from Rock Paper Shotgun: <a href=\"https://www.rockpapershotgun.com/bloodlines-2-is-more-spiritual-successor-than-sequel-to-a-a-competently-good-game-by-2004-standards-say-paradox\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;Bloodlines 2 is more &quot;spiritual successor&quot; than sequel to &quot;a competently good game by 2004 standards&quot;, say Paradox&quot;</a><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampire: The Masquerade - Bloodlines 2 won't be an &quot;open sim&quot; like the 2004 original game, according to Paradox Interactive. Now in development at The Chinese Room, <b>it'll be an action-RPG with a relatively linear story set in the World Of Darkness universe. This obviously plays to The Chinese Room's strengths - they're better known for melancholy or horrifying strolls through broken spaces than the Dishonorable massaging of intricate systems.</b> But it also reflects Paradox's view that the original Bloodlines has been &quot;mythologised&quot; a bit: people love the memory of it more than the reality, and there are aspects of the 2004 game, according to Paradox's deputy chief executive officer Mattias Lilja, that simply &quot;wouldn't fly today&quot;. </div> </div> </div>(highlights from me)<br /> <br /> So there you go... Now it's official: It will be more like a Chinese Room style of game (almost linear, story-driven experience) with a little bit of action thrown in.<br /> <br /> But I gotta wonder: When they hired Chinese Room to do this, I can't imagine they hadn't set out to do this very limited story-game with a bit of action from the start. I assume it's that type of game where you get dialogue-choices towards the end which decide what type of ending you're gonna get - but outside of that, the player's actions have no impact on the story. This also fits the talents of the Chinese Room. That's the sort of games they're famous for.<br /> <br /> And also this bit from later in the article:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If Paradox have learned anything from the past few years of delays and cancellations, it's that making or publishing games outside their traditional grand strategy dominions is a risky business. During our chat, Lilja spoke at length<b> about the need to refocus and make smaller bets on projects in future</b>. With regard to Bloodlines 2, we shouldn't expect another action-RPG from Paradox in the near future, though Paradox do expect the game to at least break even. </div> </div> </div>(highlights by me)<br /> <br /> So it seems the future for the WOD IP will be smaller games. But also: They <i>hope </i>it breaks even. I mean, what can you even say to that... A glowing endorsement it certainly is not.<br /> <br /> Here's my biggest fear: It's gonna be a very short game - but the price won't reflect that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T13:09:43-07:00","id":1543535,"title":"","content":"Sounds like Paradox is trying to undersell the quality of <i>Bloodlines 1</i>, to lower expectations about <i>Bloodlines 2</i> and its radical departure from the original's formula.<br /> <br /> Setting aside that it's throwing the original game under the bus - people have held out hope all these years because they wanted another <i>Bloodlines</i> - I would argue that people's love of the game isn't overblown. Yes, <i>Bloodlines 1</i> was a janky, barely functional mess. Let it never be said it wasn't a product of both its time and the troubled development that spawned it. But people liked the game because it was still the most archetypal World of Darkness title we've ever received. (In itself a damning indictment of every tie-in game, including the output of Paradox itself).<br /> <br /> There's a reason people rush to reinstall the game every time they hear about it. You don't do that for a game coasting solely on rose-tinted glasses.<br /> <br /> Will people be so eager to reinstall <i>Bloodlines 2</i> when that game has run its course?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T13:41:32-07:00","id":1543536,"title":"","content":"Once again: Chronicles of Darkness got smothered and ghosted for this? World of Darkness got dragged through the mud for this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T15:23:20-07:00","id":1543550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543536#post1543536\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once again: Chronicles of Darkness got smothered and ghosted for this? World of Darkness got dragged through the mud for this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path Publishing's 5th Edition supplements justify its existence.<br /> <br /> But this is not a good sign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T15:47:34-07:00","id":1543553,"title":"","content":"This is definitely out of place, but I'll say it anyway. I wish they invested in more experiences like Courts of New York, not that it was a perfect game, far from it, but I liked what was done there, despite what they did with the ending.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T15:56:45-07:00","id":1543555,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543550#post1543550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Onyx Path Publishing's 5th Edition supplements justify its existence.<br /> <br /> But this is not a good sign.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me if I\u2019m more cynical given the game line I love got cancelled with nary a word. I have zero doubt the OPP V5 books were good. That doesn\u2019t justify Paradox destroying Chronicles. Especially since I recall OPP was already developing their own fifth edition before Paradox acquired that IP.<br /> <br /> I guarantee it would have been a million times better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T18:02:33-07:00","id":1543561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543535#post1543535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like Paradox is trying to undersell the quality of <i>Bloodlines 1</i>, to lower expectations about <i>Bloodlines 2</i> and its radical departure from the original's formula.<br /> <br /> Setting aside that it's throwing the original game under the bus - people have held out hope all these years because they wanted another <i>Bloodlines</i> - I would argue that people's love of the game isn't overblown. Yes, <i>Bloodlines 1</i> was a janky, barely functional mess. Let it never be said it wasn't a product of both its time and the troubled development that spawned it. But people liked the game because it was still the most archetypal World of Darkness title we've ever received. (In itself a damning indictment of every tie-in game, including the output of Paradox itself).<br /> <br /> There's a reason people rush to reinstall the game every time they hear about it. You don't do that for a game coasting solely on rose-tinted glasses.<br /> <br /> Will people be so eager to reinstall <i>Bloodlines 2</i> when that game has run its course?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, Bloodlines was not terribly successful at release because of how buggy it was, but with the various fan-patches available, it manages to hold up extremely well. The fact that it often pops up on lists of the top 50-25 RPGs of all time, would suggest that it isn't just a matter of nostalgia. Several segments of the game (like the Malkavian playthrough or the Ocean House Hotel) are extremely unique and still get a lot of praise even by modern gaming standards. <br /> <br /> I agree that it sounds like they're trying to downplay Bloodlines 1 (&quot;Many people believe Bloodlines was a great game, but it wasn't actually very good and the only reason they believe that is due to nostalgia,&quot;) because they suspect that Bloodlines 2 will measure up pretty poorly in comparison.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-10T20:45:37-07:00","id":1543569,"title":"","content":"I think the far more telling take away is the statement that no DLC is planned for Bloodlines 2.<br /> <br /> Paradox Interactive is one of the more notorious game companies for milking DLC microtransactions out of their games. If they are publicly stating that there won't even be an attempt to monetize Bloodlines 2, then you can pretty much assume not only is the game dead on arrival with no active support, but that they want to get as far away from it as possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T13:33:23-07:00","id":1543592,"title":"","content":"The whole idea of downplaying BL 1 as being &quot;mythologized&quot; seems to imply a severe lack of understanding behind how cult classic media becomes what it is. Cult classics are usually commercial failures (or at least under performers) that pick up audiences over time because they have something that people love even with all the other options out there. Whatever that is, that thing that's &quot;mythologized,&quot; is what's actually keeping people playing/watching/modding the game two decades later. Nobody is expecting a sequel to be the original again with a fresh coat of paint, but a successful sequel needs to understand what the people that still love the original loved about it, and figure out how to bring that into a new story.<br /> <br /> We all know there are aspects of BL 1 that didn't age well even with all the fan fixes. That's why fans want a new game. But people that weren't even born when BL 1 came out wouldn't play the game now if the core experience itself was the problem.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-11T22:33:08-07:00","id":1543608,"title":"","content":"Isn't a &quot;spiritual successor&quot; usually a game that tries to recreate the gameplay of an earlier game without an official license, sometimes from the original creators? Like Dragon Age; Orings for Baldur's Gate, Arx Fatalis for Ultima Underworld, Bloodstained for Castlevania, etc.<br /> What they are describing is the exact opposite, slapping the name of a classic game because they have the rights while going in a totally different direction gameplay wise. It's false advertising.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19862-jadeite","name":"jadeite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T04:13:25-07:00","id":1543614,"title":"","content":"I don't know about false advertising, but yeah, that's kind of a weird thing to say. It's not a &quot;spiritual&quot; successor, it's a literal successor. It's Bloodlines 2, a sequel to Bloodlines 1. It's like saying Dragon Age 3 is a spiritual successor to Baldurs Gate 2. Like no, it's the same franchise.<br /> <br /> Really, I feel like it's part of the goal of downplaying expectations. &quot;It's a sequel but not a real sequel. Don't misunderstand, you're getting Bloodlines, but you're not getting <i>Bloodlines</i>.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T05:01:05-07:00","id":1543617,"title":"","content":"Well, if we're talking &quot;false advertising&quot;, the thing I would be thinking of is the time last year when they announced the game's release date and that it would be developed by the Chinese Room. They had <a href=\"https://www.paradoxinteractive.com/games/vampire-the-masquerade-bloodlines-2/news/rpg-and-narrative-stream\" target=\"_blank\">this RPG/Narrative-stream</a> for the game in late October last year where you got statements like:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Players choose Phyre\u2019s clan and gender and begin exploring a reimagined Seattle filled with compelling characters while maneuvering through complex relationships. Choices and conversations (even outfits!) shape how the environment and characters react to Phyre, changing how the story unfolds.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We are happy to share that over the coming weeks we will reveal the four clans playable at launch. The first will be revealed next week. In addition to these four clans, an additional clan will be made available via DLC. A sixth clan will appear in a unique, standalone DLC. Details on the DLCs will be shared during 2024. Some of the clans will be familiar to Bloodlines players, but some will surprise!&quot; </div> </div> </div>At this point, I think it's safer to assume that you're going to play as female Phyre and you can't change her look (outside of the clothes she's wearing). The story is pretty linear rather than responsive to player-choices. And now we know: There won't be any DLC.<br /> <br /> Additionally, I've been thinking about why the game felt so unfinished last year and why it then it wasn't a surprise when we got news of a delay this year. According to the Chinese Room, the game has been in development since 2021. And so to aim for a 2024 release-date would've been reasonable. But then there's also the part that Bloodlines 2 uses the Unreal 5 engine - which officially came out in April 2022. That switch in engine is what disrupted the development, I imagine and this is why the gameplay-reveals from last year didn't feel like it was from a game that had been in development since 2021.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T16:39:03-07:00","id":1543647,"title":"","content":"It sounds like that nobody has to much high hopes that this game will be worth the wait. At this point is there anybody with a kernel if hope left?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T16:46:24-07:00","id":1543648,"title":"","content":"<img data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"https://i.redd.it/tbh6szcnxqtd1.jpeg\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"https://i.redd.it/tbh6szcnxqtd1.jpeg\" data-thumb-url=\"https://i.redd.it/tbh6szcnxqtd1.jpeg\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-lightbox bbcode-attachment--lightbox\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> <br /> I like Male V's look.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T16:53:21-07:00","id":1543649,"title":"","content":"Yeah the male one looks a lot better","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-12-2024, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T16:54:29-07:00","id":1543650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543647#post1543647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like that nobody has to much high hopes that this game will be worth the wait. At this point is there anybody with a kernel if hope left?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair everyone thought that silent hill remake would stink so who knows?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T18:02:54-07:00","id":1543652,"title":"","content":"I think it all comes back to the lack of previews that simply show off the gameplay in action. They have had a lot of text in their dev-diaries talking about the game and very little to show off in actual footage of the game in action. That's the first thing that made me skeptical and that then culminated in the announcement of the delay recently.<br /> <br /> Male Phyre is another one of those things. We've never seen that in action and we have yet to hear the VA for this presumed alternative. Also, if you're reading dev-diaries lately, they're referring to Phyre exclusively with she/her pronouns. And I think they're doing that because there isn't gonna be an option for a male Phyre.<br /> <br /> But the whole situation is very unusual. The game isn't even out yet, it's still in development. Between now and I guess June 2025, things can theoretically still somewhat change. At the same time, though, if anybody would know what the actual state of the game is, it would be the publisher. It's of course an odd decision for the publisher to come out like this and pour cold water on all the hopes and expectations for this game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:02:09-07:00","id":1543653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543647#post1543647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like that nobody has to much high hopes that this game will be worth the wait. At this point is there anybody with a kernel if hope left?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not too much. There's a lot of potential in the idea of having the main character be a somewhat well known elder that has only recently awoken from topor. But even really good authors would find it a struggle to do justice on the concept. I have no idea if Chinese Room is going to be able to pull it off but the main character being called Phyre was already making me raise my eyebrow a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:21:56-07:00","id":1543654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543647#post1543647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It sounds like that nobody has to much high hopes that this game will be worth the wait. At this point is there anybody with a kernel if hope left?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a tricky thing to have hope since the game isn't being made for anyone in particular. It can't be too old school lest it offend the modern audience, it can't be too modern lest it insult the original fans. The company will want it to mirror the mechanics and setting of V5 to act as a gateway for new players, but the negativity around V5 verses V20 means that can be a black mark as well.<br /> <br /> A video game designer can justify a lot of changes when they try to go in a different direction, like how Resident Evil shifted from survival horror to survival action when RE4 came out. But VtM is essentially a Venn diagram of very specific things, which cease to be VtM when you swap them out or remove those aspects entirely. This is probably why it has been in development hell for so long, you can't mess with the formula too much or it breaks.<br /> <br /> Case in point, VtM Bloodhunt is a F2P battle royale game set in the WoD, but it is not a good VtM game. Not because it's a bad game, but because VtM is more than just combat. Likewise, I am somewhat critical of the VtM visual novels despite them nailing the setting and feel. The writing makes my head hurt because I routinely argue with the decisions and options presented.<br /> <br /> I think the best level of hope you can ask of people is that they will still take a look at it when/if it comes out, rather than actively ignoring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T19:29:05-07:00","id":1543657,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543653#post1543653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not too much. There's a lot of potential in the idea of having the main character be a somewhat well known elder that has only recently awoken from topor. But even really good authors would find it a struggle to do justice on the concept. I have no idea if Chinese Room is going to be able to pull it off but the main character being called Phyre was already making me raise my eyebrow a bit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if the authors make an excellent storyline, starting out as an Elder more or less violates modern video game design. An RPG means stats go up as game progress is achieved but being an Elder means you are a max stat end game build from the start. The storyline and social mechanics would have to do all the heavy lifting rather than level grinding as content. If they do something like needing to reawaken your blood potency and regain access to your high level stats and abilities, then the Elder title is more or less window dressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T20:46:07-07:00","id":1543664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543657#post1543657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if the authors make an excellent storyline, starting out as an Elder more or less violates modern video game design. An RPG means stats go up as game progress is achieved but being an Elder means you are a max stat end game build from the start. The storyline and social mechanics would have to do all the heavy lifting rather than level grinding as content. If they do something like needing to reawaken your blood potency and regain access to your high level stats and abilities, then the Elder title is more or less window dressing.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can have high generation elders or low generation neonates. Being an elder is as much about actual age as it is potency of the blood. An 11th or 12 generation vampire that's been active for 1000 years is going to be much more powerful than an brand new 8th generation neonate. Ultimately though Chinese Room makes walking simulators more similar to visual novels than typical video games. I think you'll get a few powerful disciplines to wipe out the roomful of mooks you occasionally come across, but for the most part I don't imagine the game's combat is going to reflect V5 very well.<br /> <br /> The same was more or less true for the first Bloodlines as well. The protagonist was a brand new vampire, literally sired that night and yet look at everything they were able to accomplish within a week or so. That was well outside the scope of the typical VtM neonate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-12T23:42:18-07:00","id":1543668,"title":"","content":"The previews also pretty much explained how they plan on meshing Elder with RPG mechanics: Phyre has been screwed with magically (possibly playing into the weirdness of Thin Blood Alchemy in V5 as something Phyre has no idea of from before torpor), and it's limiting power. Instead of getting stronger, you unlock blocked off power. Plus in V5 vampires do weaken with time in torpor on some level, so it's not as out of keeping with things as it would be if BL 2 was meant to follow pre-V5 assumptions.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> Though to back track to the &quot;spiritual successor&quot; bit, what's going on is usually called a &quot;Dolled-Up Installment.&quot; Though most dolled-up installments take existing media and reskin it into an existing franchise (What was released as Super Mario Bros. 2 in the US is a classic example) hoping that you can piggy back off the existing brand-associations rather than having to build up hype for an entirely new game (or movie, or whatever).<br /> <br /> I guess it's not a perfect term in this case though, because usually a dolled-up installment builds off of something unrelated that's rolled into an existing franchise, rather than deciding to give up making a normal installment with something that's going to end up like a dolled-up installment instead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T07:40:43-07:00","id":1543678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end#post1543390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The CEO saying that Bloodlines is a 'dead end' and writing off a hypothetical Bloodlines 3 isn't exactly instilling me with very good expectations for part 2. Honestly it sounds like the CEO doesn't have any interest in the WoD IP whatsoever. At this point, I'm kind of hoping they sell the IP to someone else who has more desire to work with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So assuming that pardox do decided sell the WoD IP rights to another company. Who do you think would get the rights? <br /> <br /> I personally wish that Sigune Games get the rights if only because I want to see what they would do with the WtA setting. I know I'm kinda typecasting them since they're most known for making Iron Claw which is a Fantasy Furry game and well like it or not WtA has a cult following among the fandom. But they're a quality developer in they niche as far as I know.<br /> <br /> Of course a slightly more realistic possibility is Games Workshop which as far as I know potentially suffers problems with Pardox but they felid is tabletop adjunct so management might have a vague idea on how to handle IP properly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T08:10:58-07:00","id":1543680,"title":"","content":"If Paradox sells off the IP, I hope whoever gets control of WoD decides to completely scrap and retcon V5/W5 and go back to the V20 setting as a baseline for any further future endeavors.<br /> <br /> I'm sadly not optimistic for that<br /> <br /> The only good thing to come out of the Paradox buyout was the Storyteller's Vault. Everything else, from V5 to the forced death of CofD to Bloodlines 2 shaping up to be a latter-day Duke Nukem Forever, has been an utter bane upon the WoD IP","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":25920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","user":"Matt Corleone","date":". 10-13-2024, 11:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T11:56:25-07:00","id":1543695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543680#post1543680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Paradox sells off the IP, I hope whoever gets control of WoD decides to completely scrap and retcon V5/W5 and go back to the V20 setting as a baseline for any further future endeavors</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not. I love...everything OPP did.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T13:24:46-07:00","id":1543699,"title":"","content":"Here's a good video that summarizes the situation that Paradox has found itself in:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=CptrqD2jh6c\" data-code=\"CptrqD2jh6c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/CptrqD2jh6c/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> It's more of a general look at Paradox and what this media-tour has been about. But Bloodlines 2 does come up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T15:58:43-07:00","id":1543710,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt Corleone</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543680#post1543680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If Paradox sells off the IP, I hope whoever gets control of WoD decides to completely scrap and retcon V5/W5 and go back to the V20 setting as a baseline for any further future endeavors.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyone who would do that would just end up being as bad or worse than Paradox.<br /> <br /> It is precisely this kind of depreciative treatment with the fanbase and previous material due to having a \u201cdefinite personal view\u201d of the game that got us where we are. Paradox does what they want with the IP and everyone else be damned.<br /> <br /> However you initially agree with the vision of the next one, as long as they hold this same attitude, it\u2019s a matter of time for the same mistakes to happen.<br /> <br /> WoD5 has its fans and already has a reasonable amount of material and lore. The path a new owner can take without incurring in the same errors is to either start from WoD5 and get things on track without ignoring it, or to make it into an alternative setting.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s still a long way from here. Selling the IP isn\u2019t a simple or fast thing. Who\u2019s interested? How much is it valued today? Who has an actual working plan to make this investment and then work with it?<br /> <br /> The beginning of this whole mess was an enthusiastic CEO making a costly acquisition without any idea of how it would actually use it. He had a vision of how it would be a money-making machine in the future, but none in how he would get there. And it being outside his company\u2019s main market played a huge role in this catastrophe.<br /> <br /> Now we need a company that either understands this market or really knows who does, but then this buyer will have to both be able to make the investment and have an actual plan to make it worth it in a timely fashion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":3},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T16:04:34-07:00","id":1543711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543664#post1543664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can have high generation elders or low generation neonates. Being an elder is as much about actual age as it is potency of the blood. An 11th or 12 generation vampire that's been active for 1000 years is going to be much more powerful than an brand new 8th generation neonate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Elder is a function of XP accrued and invested which is a function of time active, rather than expressly being about Generation. Though to be a hint pedantic, I will point out that as the starting generation goes down the number of starter discipline dots goes up. So age can mean that not only does the character have more XP, but they also have more dots. Obviously, this only starts applying around Generation 8 to 7 mark. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543664#post1543664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same was more or less true for the first Bloodlines as well. The protagonist was a brand new vampire, literally sired that night and yet look at everything they were able to accomplish within a week or so. That was well outside the scope of the typical VtM neonate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree that such things are unlikely, but I feel that it is more of a function of game play and XP gain than a hard cap of what a neonate can do. If you play in the table top game every day, your XP gain after a year IRL will put you on par with Elders stat wise, and since Backgrounds gain be gained without XP costs those can change to an even greater degree. On the other hand if you play once a month, your XP level will be a neonate pretty much forever. Bloodlines 1 has a character growth rate of a daily player while everyone else is a monthly player.<br /> <br /> It is also worth noting that because the Neonate has nothing, they are free to work for anyone, they can bounce between factions, they have yet to work out who is just being grumpy as opposed to being a true enemy. Once you start building a power base, lay down some roots, and invest in your faction, then you are more hesitant to rock the boat as much as a neonate can afford to, so it is easy to see why a Neonate could accomplish more than an Elder assuming they are willing to risk their unlives to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T18:13:04-07:00","id":1543719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543710#post1543710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The beginning of this whole mess was an enthusiastic CEO making a costly acquisition without any idea of how it would actually use it. He had a vision of how it would be a money-making machine in the future, but none in how he would get there. And it being outside his company\u2019s main market played a huge role in this catastrophe.<br /> <br /> Now we need a company that either understands this market or really knows who does, but then this buyer will have to both be able to make the investment and have an actual plan to make it worth it in a timely fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's right which is why I think Games Workshop is one of the more realistic buyers of the IP. They're have the money to buy it since they're the biggest arguably THE table top wargaming developer in the world. And more importantly GW does have experience experience with publishing TTRPGS with Only War and Dark heresy which are fondly remembered by they players. <br /> <br /> Though I should note that GW has spilt from they usual TTRPG's devs in 2017 and they recent TTRPG Wrath and Glory has had a rough lunch as far as I can tell. <br /> <br /> Of course there's also the multimedia push for they flagship property Warhammer 40K that's are primarily focused on videogames.<br /> <br /> Like as far I can tell all the recent 40K games has lunched more or less smoothly and has met with mostly positive receptions from the public which is more than I can say for Bloodlines 2. So a WOD game is in decently good hands if GW decides to back it.<br /> <br /> Of course it's not all sun shine and roses since GW are infamous litigious when it comes to fan products especially after Warhammer + lunched and the fan base has made plenty of jokes on they money gouging when it comes to minture sales. And of course there's nothing preventing GW (or Paradox for that matter). To just sit on the IP and Do nothing...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-13T18:59:23-07:00","id":1543722,"title":"","content":"IMHO, the best way to handle WoD5 is to retcon it and declare it non-canon and support WoD20 from that point on BUT also allow V5 to be supported as an alternate setting that is non-canon but won't be completely cancelled either, so V5 fans can still get their fix on places like Storytellers Vault<br /> <br /> Have OPP work on Chronicles and Renegade can work on WoD5, but have it be treated as a &quot;What If?&quot; setting or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T08:03:26-07:00","id":1543750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrornX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543719#post1543719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's right which is why I think Games Workshop is one of the more realistic buyers of the IP. They're have the money to buy it since they're the biggest arguably THE table top wargaming developer in the world. And more importantly GW does have experience experience with publishing TTRPGS with Only War and Dark heresy which are fondly remembered by they players.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to confirm, would this be the same Games Workshop which is currently mass leasing out their IPs with little to no quality control so that there are a ton of bad spin off video games? Or is this the same GW which is desecrating their own lore for the sake DEI/ESRG money? Either way it would be the death of WoD.<br /> <br /> DEI VtM.... it would make the coven of lesbian space witches producing children through immaculate Force conception from the Acolyte tv show look tame by comparison. I can see the V6 rewrite in my head even now. All male vampires are called Cainites and inherently are seen as abhorrent and are blamed for all the bad things vampires theoretically do. The female vampires are all Lilluns since they recognize Lilith as their creator rather than Caine. Well if nothing else that would simplify the explanation of the vampire setting down to just two clans/bloodlines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":8},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T10:13:40-07:00","id":1543763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543750#post1543750\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to confirm, would this be the same Games Workshop which is currently mass leasing out their IPs with little to no quality control so that there are a ton of bad spin off video games? Or is this the same GW which is desecrating their own lore for the sake DEI/ESRG money? Either way it would be the death of WoD.<br /> <br /> DEI VtM.... it would make the coven of lesbian space witches producing children through immaculate Force conception from the Acolyte tv show look tame by comparison. I can see the V6 rewrite in my head even now. All male vampires are called Cainites and inherently are seen as abhorrent and are blamed for all the bad things vampires theoretically do. The female vampires are all Lilluns since they recognize Lilith as their creator rather than Caine. Well if nothing else that would simplify the explanation of the vampire setting down to just two clans/bloodlines.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Banned from the thread.</b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T10:53:46-07:00","id":1543768,"title":"","content":"Before anything else, I don't really see WoD making a comeback until D&amp;D 5e dies and stops choking out gaming stores. Having every TTRPG initiate wanting to adapt everything to 5e, and refusing to move on to any other systems when that inevitably fails, has been disastrous to the hobby as a whole for a while now.<br /> <br /> I think we'll be heading for another TTRPG winter long before anything gets better. Until then, AI might become good enough to fill out missing spots in a group. The result will probably be funny if nothing else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd22","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T11:43:23-07:00","id":1543773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543768#post1543768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Before anything else, I don't really see WoD making a comeback until D&amp;D 5e dies and stops choking out gaming stores. Having every TTRPG initiate wanting to adapt everything to 5e, and refusing to move on to any other systems when that inevitably fails, has been disastrous to the hobby as a whole for a while now.<br /> <br /> I think we'll be heading for another TTRPG winter long before anything gets better. Until then, AI might become good enough to fill out missing spots in a group. The result will probably be funny if nothing else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evil such as D&amp;D 5e does not simply die. It must be slain. Also, AI isn't AI, and the amount of power it would require to do anything remotely good would require a renaissance in nuclear reactor production <i>and</i> cooling systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T17:08:34-07:00","id":1543802,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543773#post1543773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Evil such as D&amp;D 5e does not simply die. It must be slain. Also, AI isn't AI, and the amount of power it would require to do anything remotely good <b>would require a renaissance in nuclear reactor production <i>and</i> cooling systems.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Already happening. Every major AI company(Google, Microsoft, and Open AI at least) have been making moves to get the rights to have personal nuclear reactors built specifically to power their training centers. There are also already a number of new, proven cooling technologies that are currently held back by economy of scale and more on the way, including revolutions in 3 dimensional chip design that're already in the pipeline.<br /> <br /> the tech for the next couple AI revolutions is already out, it's just bottle-necked by issues related to supply-lines, political tensions, and the slow wind-up endemic to mass production.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-14T17:21:56-07:00","id":1543803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543802#post1543802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Already happening. Every major AI company(Google, Microsoft, and Open AI at least) have been making moves to get the rights to have personal nuclear reactors built specifically to power their training centers. There are also already a number of new, proven cooling technologies that are currently held back by economy of scale and more on the way, including revolutions in 3 dimensional chip design that're already in the pipeline.<br /> <br /> the tech for the next couple AI revolutions is already out, it's just bottle-necked by issues related to supply-lines, political tensions, and the slow wind-up endemic to mass production.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, all you need to do is pay those companies giant piles of money to replace one person in your ttrpg group and only play in the bowels of the power and processing station. And then still get hit with the uncanny valley effect because machine learning doesn't produce what's compatible with biological thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:06:12-07:00","id":1543860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543803#post1543803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Great, all you need to do is pay those companies giant piles of money to replace one person in your ttrpg group and only play in the bowels of the power and processing station. And then still get hit with the uncanny valley effect because machine learning doesn't produce what's compatible with biological thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>You only need giant amounts of power and computing to build+train the model initially. After that you can run most models locally on a decent gaming PC.<br /> <br /> Even money isn't an issue for the patient. Large expensive private models only hold a monopoly for less than 6 months after public release before the crowdsourced free models catch up to(and in many cases outperform) them.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that we don't actually live in WoD or Shadowrun. Attempts at cyberpunk dystopias fall apart rather quickly IRL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T08:20:42-07:00","id":1543865,"title":"","content":"I think the most accurate description for AI technology in the present is: unsustainable, untenable and unprofitable. Anything else is delusional. There's a <a href=\"https://www.wheresyoured.at/oai-business/\" target=\"_blank\">great article by Ed Zitron</a> called &quot;OpenAI is bad business&quot; about the wasteful nature of the AI industry and in this case OpenAI in particular.<br /> <br /> Google, Microsoft and OpenAI fighting over it is less a fight and more a contest over who can set more money on fire for nothing in return. The only reason companies like Google and Microsoft will survive where OpenAI will not is because those two can stomach the obvious unprofitability of present-day AI-technology. Remember Meta and all that VR-nonsense? The current technology is just the latest iteration of that kind of delusion in the tech-sector.<br /> <br /> Paradox investing in AI technology would be a disaster. The only thing you would get out of that is Paradox declaring bankruptcy...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T09:24:15-07:00","id":1543870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543860#post1543860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You only need giant amounts of power and computing to build+train the model initially. After that you can run most models locally on a decent gaming PC.<br /> <br /> Even money isn't an issue for the patient. Large expensive private models only hold a monopoly for less than 6 months after public release before the crowdsourced free models catch up to(and in many cases outperform) them.<br /> <br /> Don't forget that we don't actually live in WoD or Shadowrun. Attempts at cyberpunk dystopias fall apart rather quickly IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trying to get human-like output out of a program is dependent on energy-hungry, power-wasting hot hardware, so no, you couldn't run it on a decent gaming PC. You'd be dealing with something like the VEGA complex in DOOM 2016, except nowhere near as effective, because VEGA - and its cooling system - is powered on unlimited magical energy from another universe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-15T14:54:38-07:00","id":1543913,"title":"","content":"So... since Paradox isn't talking about dumping billions into propping up the AI bubble... maybe we can take this to the Off-Topic forum?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\u2615","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T00:01:43-07:00","id":1544261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1543710#post1543710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anyone who would do that would just end up being as bad or worse than Paradox.<br /> <br /> It is precisely this kind of depreciative treatment with the fanbase and previous material due to having a \u201cdefinite personal view\u201d of the game that got us where we are. Paradox does what they want with the IP and everyone else be damned.<br /> <br /> However you initially agree with the vision of the next one, as long as they hold this same attitude, it\u2019s a matter of time for the same mistakes to happen.<br /> <br /> WoD5 has its fans and already has a reasonable amount of material and lore. The path a new owner can take without incurring in the same errors is to either start from WoD5 and get things on track without ignoring it, or to make it into an alternative setting.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s still a long way from here. Selling the IP isn\u2019t a simple or fast thing. Who\u2019s interested? How much is it valued today? Who has an actual working plan to make this investment and then work with it?<br /> <br /> The beginning of this whole mess was an enthusiastic CEO making a costly acquisition without any idea of how it would actually use it. He had a vision of how it would be a money-making machine in the future, but none in how he would get there. And it being outside his company\u2019s main market played a huge role in this catastrophe.<br /> <br /> Now we need a company that either understands this market or really knows who does, but then this buyer will have to both be able to make the investment and have an actual plan to make it worth it in a timely fashion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet sometimes a brutal retcon is critical for a brand. D&amp;D's Second Sundering effectively undid almost the entire Fourth Edition and its metaplot, and in fact allowed it to launch the most successful edition ever.<br /> <br /> You don't need a retcon-meta, where it says \u201cthis never happened.\u201d You use two or three narrative devices to get things back on a better track","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T03:51:32-07:00","id":1544271,"title":"","content":"Another option is to give up on making VtM/WoD about &quot;now&quot; and just have the default setting be the tail end of 1999. While that's 25 years ago from now, it is both a fairly pivotal era in modern history, and we have a lot more insight into what's going to matter now. It plays into the nostalgia of the WoD's original run (and it would hardly be the first time present media explores the past), with foresight into how to direct the games to what will still be relevant later.<br /> <br /> It also gives you lots of freedom to branch out in lots of directions and thus unify the player base. Does Y2K turn out to be a huge deal and the WoD explodes into a gonzo dark fantasy? There can be books exploring that. Does the WoD continue to mirror own our fairly closely as the powers that be ride the ups and downs of human history as they always have? Sure, explore that. Does the upheavals in human society lead to upheavals in supernatural societies that forces them to adapt to new eras? Do that too. This also drastically frees up the brand for different media, because anything after 1999 becomes a self-contained possible future for the WoD; whether is be one book, or a series of video games, or whatever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T15:45:47-07:00","id":1544312,"title":"","content":"Perhaps instead of 1999 it can be closer to 2003 or 2004, with the option for a longer burn if necessary. That'd match the end dates of the original WoD run. Y2K WoD could be a special case &quot;fast burn&quot; book that's part of the theoretical line but as a surprising early start to the end. It would also tamp down on the comparisons to The Matrix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T15:54:50-07:00","id":1544314,"title":"","content":"1999 makes it easier on having things for the 1e/2e fans that want to see where the Week of Nightmares blows up the Masquerade instead of the Camarilla and Technocracy successfully covering it up. It also means some contentious things (like Hunter the Reckoning) aren't set in stone of how they manifested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T16:04:14-07:00","id":1544315,"title":"","content":"The one thing I'm sure of is that you need to get away from this idea of &quot;In the past, the WOD-setting was our present-day but darker. Now the setting for WOD5E should just be the real world. Things are just that bad.&quot; Nothing was gained from that idea. At least with a darker version of reality, you had a worthwhile setting to play out Urban Fantasy scenarios. The idea that you don't need that because you feel bad about the real world is a bad concept. If you want a game that addresses these real-world-concepts... create that game. The WOD-games are about being vampires, werewolves, demons etc. It will never be able to reflect the real world.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T17:08:50-07:00","id":1544324,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1544271#post1544271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is to give up on making VtM/WoD about &quot;now&quot; and just have the default setting be the tail end of 1999. While that's 25 years ago from now, it is both a fairly pivotal era in modern history, and we have a lot more insight into what's going to matter now. It plays into the nostalgia of the WoD's original run (and it would hardly be the first time present media explores the past), with foresight into how to direct the games to what will still be relevant later.<br /> <br /> It also gives you lots of freedom to branch out in lots of directions and thus unify the player base. Does Y2K turn out to be a huge deal and the WoD explodes into a gonzo dark fantasy? There can be books exploring that. Does the WoD continue to mirror own our fairly closely as the powers that be ride the ups and downs of human history as they always have? Sure, explore that. Does the upheavals in human society lead to upheavals in supernatural societies that forces them to adapt to new eras? Do that too. This also drastically frees up the brand for different media, because anything after 1999 becomes a self-contained possible future for the WoD; whether is be one book, or a series of video games, or whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this idea a lot, actually<br /> <br /> Basically, reset it to the status quo of the Revised Edition corebook and have the more contentious metaplot issues like Independent Gangrel, the Week of Nightmares, Ur-Shulgi and the Assamite Schism (tbh, I refuse to use the term &quot;Banu Haqim&quot;, fuck that V5 shit) and so forth be treated as having just plain not happened (but nothing prevents an ST from incorporating them into their own games)<br /> <br /> V20 took this approach when it first launched and I'd say the &quot;metaplot agnostic&quot; approach that Parawolf seems to loathe so much is a major key for why it was so successful. All the prior editions and their commonly associated styles were given a seat at the table and treated equally and fairly.<br /> <br /> Though whereas V20 simply took back the most egregious decisions of the Achilli regime by acting like they never happened and just updated the setting to the 2010's, a good V6 would be an explicit late 90's/early 2000's period piece.<br /> <br /> Given the popularity of the &quot;Y2K Aesthetic&quot; online and how it's popular for both nostalgic Gen X and Millennials as well as Zoomers and Gen Alpha kids who just find that era aesthetically cool compared to the bland corporate hipster minimalist aesthetics of today, acting like V5 never happened and just making V6 a &quot;Y2K Era&quot; period piece might be the best decision.<br /> <br /> Just go all out, revert back to old names and old settings, make it an explicit period piece and everything. Go the extra mile to lean into that late 90's/early 2000's edge and &quot;Rule of Cool&quot; mindset. Go full unironic &quot;trenchcoats &amp; katanas&quot; mall goth.<br /> <br /> Have the metaplot stuff from Revised, Beckett's Jyhad Diary, and V5 be treated as potential alternate settings or options for ST's to use (alongside other plot hooks) as opposed to hard setting facts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm just a trans guy and gaming fan, unabashed hedonist and unusually upbeat nihilist, fairly laid back. He/Him.<br /> <br /> If everything is political, then nothing is!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25920-matt-corleone","name":"Matt Corleone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25920_8.webp","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"393"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T17:43:39-07:00","id":1544327,"title":"","content":"I believe that the different metaplots and the need to keep each splat both unique, yet still connected, is something that World of Darkness was groundbreaking for. Other game lines had brought metaplot to the forefront (Battletech, Shadowrun, Cyberpunk, to name a few), but none had the ambition for the variety of stories that the WOD had.<br /> <br /> <b>I think it failed miserably on an objective level but that failure SUBJECTIVELY made the original World of Darkness so beloved to so many and created the interesting culture that surrounds it to this day.</b><br /> <br /> The COMBINED World of Darkness is a mess. Even the original game lines in and of themselves were a nightmare when it came to cohesiveness, balance, and consistency. Vampire, being the oldest, definitely evolved the most, having to integrate each new paradigm shift brought on by a new splat. As the most popular, it had to be relevant with each new game and also evolve within itself to sell more books. This patchwork of contradictions, errors, and logical backflips is a gold mine for an internet subculture to dig into and analyze, hypothesize, and argue about. It is what killed an objectively more cohesive and consistent successor (nWOD/COD) and created the &quot;generation gap&quot; between 1e-20Ae lore/metaplot fans and the current developers because 5e is taking a very different approach to lore, metaplot, and interaction between the splats.<br /> <br /> The thing is, I'm not sure what you could do now with the World of Darkness as it existed up through the end of Revised. It had, developmentally, reached the end of its lifespan. Mechanically or conceptually, there was nothing new in its future, just the perpetuation of the metaplot. It would become akin to the Rolling Stones: chugging along decades after relevance performing &quot;greatest hits&quot; tours. There's nothing wrong with that but it's artistically stagnant. Hanging out in newer gaming spaces, I am realizing that the kids playing 5e are playing a very different game than what I played in 1991 by candlelight with Joy Division playing in the background. The game has moved on from us old-heads and I am here for it. I never would have thought about some of the directions the game is going these days and exploring them has been great.<br /> <br /> When we say &quot;this is what Paradox should do,&quot; we're old men yelling at clouds. Paradox is going to do what they think will make them money and what we think is irrelevant to that. I am perfectly content to be the old man standing in the back of the punk rock show, only half understanding what these kids are doing these days but loving the energy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6423-higgipedia","name":"higgipedia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6423_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"53"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T17:59:05-07:00","id":1544329,"title":"","content":"Vampire didn't really change shit in response to the other games. It had funhouse, theme-park versions of the other games' characters as antagonists in the back that stayed more or less the same for the entire run. The other games, meanwhile, had their own themes and matured in different directions. Werewolf discarded most notions of Personal Horror in exchange for Splatter. Mage flat out refused to engage with their existence as horrific and declared it wondrous. Wraith went in even harder. Changeling was maudlin but still hopeful - approaching things from an angle similar to Mage, but more maudlin.<br /> <br /> The reason why the &quot;whole line&quot; was a mess was because you weren't supposed to throw everything together; the books really did not like it and the character types clashes with each other fiercely, with a few exceptions (ghosts can fit in the background of anything, changelings can get along somewhat well with werewolves and other werebeasts).<br /> <br /> And if 5e changed anything, it's to being a stifling, One True Way as canon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T18:57:25-07:00","id":1544332,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1544315#post1544315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The one thing I'm sure of is that you need to get away from this idea of &quot;In the past, the WOD-setting was our present-day but darker. Now the setting for WOD5E should just be the real world. Things are just that bad.&quot; Nothing was gained from that idea. At least with a darker version of reality, you had a worthwhile setting to play out Urban Fantasy scenarios. The idea that you don't need that because you feel bad about the real world is a bad concept. If you want a game that addresses these real-world-concepts... create that game. The WOD-games are about being vampires, werewolves, demons etc. It will never be able to reflect the real world.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hard agree. The darkness of our Real Life isn't as sexy or exciting as the darkness of the World of Darkness. It's not a measure of degree, but in fact of type.<br /> <br /> People play the World of Darkness because the Powers That Be are vampires or cultists to eldritch horrors of primordial decay. You know, people you can and are expected to put a katana through at the earliest opportunity. Meanwhile, the evil Powers That Be in Real Life...you're not allowed to put katanas through, and it wouldn't necessarily fix the systemic problems even if you could. (Though putting the fear of mass revolt in the hearts of billionaires and despots certainly wouldn't hurt; for legal reasons, I'm advised to append the rider &quot;In Minecraft&quot; to this statement. Wink wink, nudge nudge).<br /> <br /> Making the World of Darkness just...our world, but with shittier supernaturals in the background is just less fun. Worse, it makes the whole exercise <i>depressing</i>. <br /> <br /> I don't need to be a Werewolf to sadly sit on the sidelines while the earth dies, without any legal recourse to stop it. I already have that in Real Life.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T20:01:17-07:00","id":1544334,"title":"","content":"Don't get me wrong. I really like the idea of setting Vampire in the 90s. It's a Chronicle idea I've wanted to do for a while now, where the game starts in 1991 (the year Vampire was released) and going forward from there. I think it would be fun, and a way to sort of dig into the entire vibe of the 90s with the benefit of hindsight.<br /> <br /> That said, I can't in good conscience sign off on making the 90s the default era of World of Darkness. Simply because the default should be &quot;Current Year&quot;, as a jumping on point for new players. There would need to be a good reason to set a game specifically outside the present. Call of Cthulhu, by default, takes place in the same general era as Lovecraft's stories, for genre consistency. Same with Ars Magica, which heavily relies on the conceit of exploring medieval society and its esoteric worldview.<br /> <br /> Whereas while the World of Darkness is an extremely 90s setting, it has grown and changed with the times. It WAS set in Current Year when it came out, and at least tried to be &quot;Modern&quot;. Always has been. Dips into earlier eras explored both those eras, and the timelessness of the vampire (and human) experience.<br /> <br /> If anything, there should definitely be a VtM supplement that specifically examines the 90s as a milieu in and of itself. Much like how <i>New Wave Requiem</i> was a sourcebook for running Vampire: The Requiem in the 80s. Have the 90s setting exist alongside Dark Ages Vampire and Victorian Age Vampire. The main game would explore how vampires work &quot;now&quot;, while the supplement(s) cover(s) how vampires work in the age of katanas &amp; trenchcoats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-19T22:37:55-07:00","id":1544342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1543390-paradox-ceo-says-bloodlines-is-a-dead-end?p=1544271#post1544271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another option is to give up on making VtM/WoD about &quot;now&quot; and just have the default setting be the tail end of 1999. While that's 25 years ago from now, it is both a fairly pivotal era in modern history, and we have a lot more insight into what's going to matter now. It plays into the nostalgia of the WoD's original run (and it would hardly be the first time present media explores the past), with foresight into how to direct the games to what will still be relevant later.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's basically what Relentless age did. hsienfan explicitly set time period for the game is 1998 and from what I've read on they <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/kindred-of-the-east-the-relentless-age-live-drafting-a-final-reboot.893999/\" target=\"_blank\">Rpg.net posts</a> about the game they're reasoning for that choice is that simply the period fit the tone of the game. And from what I've seen they're changeling project &quot;In The Realm of Gods and Dreams&quot; takes place in the same time period.<br /> <br /> Also on a related note the soon to be released Werewolf the Essentials has the apocalypse start in 1976 and end on 1984 and the current playable time period is a decade from then (so around 1994). <br /> <br /> I feel like it's a start of a trend for WoD fan writers to set they games as period peaces...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25848-mrornx","name":"MrornX","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"418"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}